EXTERNAL chose(knot)

// [draft]
=== workbench ===
Uncle Karim, how much for all the work? Name a number, don't be shy. #salma
Not a penny. This is the [[Hajjeh]] Im Khalil's café. #karim
That won't do. Every job gets an invoice, and I want everything in writing. #lana
Then write “paid long ago”. I was a boy learning the trade from my master, and the Hajjeh never let me go hungry a day. #karim
All right. From today, your plate and your cup are on us. #salma #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== dallah_shelf ===
One, two, three… six. There were seven! #salma #surprised
I made it like my master's old shelf, for seven dallahs. And the last place, the little one, is empty. #karim
The little one… Teta's little [[dallah]] isn't here. #salma #sad
Maybe it broke, or someone took it. Not a problem, we'll buy another. #lana
There is no other, Lana. That's the one nobody but Teta ever poured from. #salma
-> END

// [draft]
=== counter_repair ===
Hold on, boss… there's something carved under the counter. #karim #surprised
“Subhi, 1974.” That's my master's hand. I'd know it among a hundred. #karim
Your master built the counter? I never knew. #salma #surprised
And under it, in pencil: “Bless your hands.” That's the Hajjeh's writing. #karim #sad
Wood remembers who treated it well. Fifty years, and it's kept her words. #karim
-> END

// [draft]
=== small_dallah ===
Here. I polished it. It's been with me since the first night. #lana
The little dallah! Uncle, look, it's back. #salma #surprised
{
- chose("dallahs") == "ask":
    You asked me about her on your first day, and I sent you to her notebooks. But this story isn't in any notebook. #abu_fadi
- else:
    I promised you a story about her, my girl, and said not today. Well, today's the day. #abu_fadi
}
It was hers alone… except for two little girls. She'd put her hand over yours, and you'd pour together. #abu_fadi #smile
That's why I took it. I wanted to remember her hand. #lana #sad
-> END

// [draft]
=== frames ===
An envelope in Teta's writing: “Opening day, 1974. Don't throw these away.” And inside… pieces of a photo. #salma #surprised
Oh, the shame! On my children's lives, I'm the one who tore it! #samira #surprised
I was a little girl, and I came out scowling in it. Your Teta never said a word to me… she just picked up every piece. #samira
If all the pieces are here, then the big frame is hers. #karim
We'll put it back the way it was, [[Khalto]]. Scowl and all. #salma #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== photo_frame ===
The frame's ready, and the glass is new. All it needs is the photo. #karim
Shall we put it together? I'll take the edges, you take the faces. #lana
Deal. Let's see who was here on the very first day. #salma #smile
-> END

// [draft]
=== m4_lead ===
See that hand holding a cup? That's mine. I was in the photo too. #abu_fadi #smile
And my master was behind the camera. He used to say: “Nobody move. A photo outlives us all.” #karim
-> END

// [draft]
=== m4_intro ===
Step back a little, everyone. I want all the woodwork to show. #karim_master_1974
Master Subhi, photograph the people, not the wood! #teta_young #smile
And the first customer, where does he stand, Im Khalil? #fadi_young
In front, with his cup in his hand. And you, Samira, my heart, no scowling! #teta_young
Samira, smile for the master, God bless you. #samira_mother_1974
-> END

// [draft]
=== m4_perfect ===
Every face in its place, and nobody blinked. This photo will last. #karim_master_1974
-> END

// [draft]
=== m4_ok ===
Never mind if someone blinked. What matters is we're all in it. #teta_young
-> END

// [draft]
=== m4_outro ===
And you, Master? You made all this woodwork, and there's no place for you in the photo? #teta_young
The one who takes the photo isn't in it, ma'am. But I'll take one of my work on its own, for me. #karim_master_1974
Subhi photographed the counter on its own and hung it in his workshop. Years later, a boy named Karim learned the trade beneath it. #sys
-> END

// [draft]
=== m4_return ===
That photo of the counter is still in my workshop. I grew up looking at it. #karim
And there's me, look! Scowling, just like I told you. #samira #smile
You were all here from the very first day. And the photo's back where it belongs. #salma #smile
-> END
